# Typography scale (4px steps)

Prefer sizes on a **4px grid**. Do not use critical UI text smaller than **12px**.

| Role | Size | Tailwind (prefer) |
|------|------|-------------------|
| H1 / page titles | **32px–40px** | `text-3xl` (30) → prefer `text-[32px]` / `text-4xl` (36) / `text-[40px]` |
| H2 / section headings | **24px** | `text-2xl` |
| H3 / subsection headings | **20px** | `text-xl` |
| Body text | **16px** | `text-base` |
| Buttons / nav links | **16px** | `text-base` |
| Captions / helper text | **12px** | `text-xs` |

## Rules

- Avoid off-grid sizes for UI copy: **14px** (`text-sm`), **18px** (`text-lg`), and other odd px values unless matching an existing design-system token that cannot change yet.
- Captions and helpers: `text-xs` (12px). Never go below 12px for anything users must read (errors, labels, limits, legal-critical notes).
- Page titles: keep within 32–40px; do not jump to huge display sizes unless the surface is intentionally marketing/hero-only.
- When editing existing UI, migrate nearby off-scale text toward this scale rather than introducing new `text-sm` / `text-lg` usage.
